SRR19415546	PRJNA842576	SRP377183	SAMN28679549	SRX15470021	Homo sapiens	Donor1_CAR_Stim5 [FB5B_S109_L004_R1_001]	Donor1_CAR_Stim5 [FB5B_S109_L004_R1_001]	Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6199069: Donor1_CAR_Stim5 [FB5B_S109_L004_R1_001] Homo sapiens RNA-Seq	RNA-Seq	TRANSCRIPTOMIC	cDNA	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina NovaSeq 6000	T cells were subjected to the repeated stimulation assay in 24-well plates, transferring T cells to freshly seeded cancer cells every 48 hours. Cultured T cells were sorted after each stimulation using BD FACSAria Fusion to obtain a pure population of NY-ESO-1 multimer positive cells T cells from the co-cultures with target cancer cells, and resuspended in TRI Reagent (Sigma, Cat.# T9424). Total RNA was extracted using Direct-zol RNA MicroPrep kit (Zymo research, Cat.# R2061) For paired-end samples, RNA-seq libraries were prepared by Oligo dT enrichment followed by a stranded Illumina library prep protocol with the KAPA mRNA HyperPrep kit (Kapa Biosystems, KK8580). Libraries were checked for quality on an AATI Fragment analyzer (Agilent, DNF-935–1000), quantified using the Illumina Quant Universal qPCR Mix (Kapa Biosystems, KK4824), and pooled evenly at 3nM. For single read samples (RASA2KO and CTRL Stim5), batch-Tag-seq protocol was used (PMID 27037501).	46169641	13943231582	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR194/046/SRR19415546/SRR19415546_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR194/046/SRR19415546/SRR19415546_2.fastq.gz	e5463d3eebd611ee04c4345689eb272a;ff52759d1199715628da57fa5edce76b	3368448375;3404182078
